  "answer_text": "Great question \u2014 and like GIF, \"doge\" is actually a surprisingly contested pronunciation! Here's a breakdown:\n\n---\n\n## How to Pronounce \"Doge\"\n\n### \ud83c\udfc6 The Most Widely Accepted: **\"DOHJ\"** (rhymes with *vogue* or *loge*)\nThe most commonly accepted pronunciation of Doge is **\"dohj\"** (IPA: /do\u028a\u0292/). This was confirmed by Dogecoin's co-creator Jackson Palmer, who said the name was inspired by the animated series *Homestar Runner*. In one of the episodes, a character spells out D-O-G-E and another character reads it as \"dohj\" (/do\u028a\u0292/).\n\n---\n\n### The Main Pronunciations in Use\n\nAccording to Wikipedia, the meme can be pronounced **/do\u028a\u0292/** (DOHZH), **/do\u028ad\u0292/** (DOHJ), or **/do\u028a\u0261/** (DOHG).\n\nHere's what each sounds like:\n\n| Pronunciation | Sounds Like | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| **DOHJ** /do\u028ad\u0292/ | \"dodge\" with a long O | Very common; how Strong Bad said it in *Homestar Runner* |\n| **DOHZH** /do\u028a\u0292/ | like the \"ge\" in *beige* | Most heard in media; also how the historical Venetian ruler is sometimes pronounced |\n| **DOHG** /do\u028a\u0261/ | rhymes with *vogue* or *rogue* | Based on the logic that the \"e\" just lengthens the vowel, like \"mop \u2192 mope\" |\n| **DOH-geh** | two syllables, like \"doggy\" | Less common; used by some who see it as a pseudo-Japanese/lolspeak word |\n\n---\n\n### The Origin of the Confusion\n\nThe \"DOHJ\" pronunciation is widely believed to have originated with a Tumblr user who submitted a computer-read audio file to a site called \"Your Daily Doge,\" though it's also been attributed to a 2005 puppet episode of *Homestar Runner*, in which Homestar misspells \"dog\" as D-O-G-E.\n\nIt's also the same way that one pronounces the name of the chief magistrate of Venice, so it's entirely possible that this pronunciation just feels older and more secure to the people who use it.\n\n---\n\n### Bottom Line\nIf you want to say it the way the **creators of Dogecoin intended**, go with **\"DOHJ\"**. But much like GIF, there's no single universally enforced pronunciation \u2014 so pick your camp and defend it! \ud83d\udc15",
